<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">European Union</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The European Union is a political and economic union of European states, developed from the European communities founded in the 1950s. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charlemagne">Charlemagne</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carolingian-empire">Carolingian Empire</a>, which united much of western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>, are often invoked as symbolic forerunners of European unity in discussions of the EU.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/european-union.jpg" alt="European Union" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Verdy p, -xfi-, Paddu, Nightstallion, Funakoshi, Jeltz, Dbenbenn, Zscout370 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Europe.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>It adopted the euro under a monetary agreement with the <b>European Union</b> signed in 2011, introduced corporate and personal income taxes in the 2010s and ended banking secrecy.</blockquote><a href="/empire/andorra">Andorra · Into the Present</a></li><li><blockquote>…the first Christian state into a republic at war from its birth: it won Nagorno-Karabakh in 1994, lost it in 2020 and 2023, overthrew its entrenched rulers in the 'velvet revolution' of 2018, and now turns from Russia towards the <b>European Union</b> and a peace deal with Azerbaijan.</blockquote><a href="/empire/armenia">Armenia · Into the Present</a></li><li><blockquote>Its weight abroad rests on energy: the Southern Gas Corridor from Shah Deniz to Europe is meant to reduce the <b>European Union</b>'s dependence on Russian gas.</blockquote><a href="/empire/azerbaijan">Azerbaijan · Global &amp; Regional Impact</a></li><li><blockquote>The idea inspired the Holy Roman Empire, the medieval papacy's universal claims and later visions of European unity, including the <b>European Union</b>.</blockquote><a href="/empire/carolingian-empire">Carolingian Empire · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li><li><blockquote>Today the republic covers 357,022 square kilometres and has 84.7 million people by the 2023 census, the most populous member state of the <b>European Union</b>; Berlin is the largest city and the Ruhr the largest urban area.</blockquote><a href="/empire/federal-republic-of-germany">Federal Republic of Germany · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>The Association Agreement with the <b>European Union</b>, signed in June 2014, entered into force on 1 July 2016, visa-free travel to the EU followed in 2017, and on 3 March 2022, days after Russia invaded Ukraine, Georgia applied for membership with Ukraine and Moldova; the European Council granted…</blockquote><a href="/empire/georgia">Georgia · Global &amp; Regional Impact</a></li></ul></section>
